; 07b-only-exit-is-a-crash.l0 -- the one way an L0 program can exit nonzero.
;
; Companion to 07. This checks and runs: it takes the head of an empty list
; on purpose. The process exits 70 with "l0: runtime error: head of empty
; list" on stderr, and whatever the program meant to say is lost. There is no
; way to choose the status or the message.

(def main ((input (list int))) (list int)
  (head (nil (list int))))
